Subject: [PATCH 105/105] doc: describe P2MR leaf version 0xe2 and its lattice
 tripwire outputs

doc/p2mr-lattice-tripwire.md describes where leaf version 0xe2 executes,
the lattice tripwire outputs and what present means for them, the NUMS key
and how it is computed, the execution rules and their order, the rescue
lane in that leaf version (elliptic curve checks rescuable as in 0xe0, the
disabled ML-DSA-44 check not), the activation on each chain and that it is
not active on Ark-0 until its height and outputs are decided, the policy,
with the 80-byte limit at depth zero that holds before activation too
(rule 4T-4) and why, the RPC and the logs, and the tests. doc/p2mr.md points to it.
